<Base lang="en" noindex title="Caldrew | Press" description="Caldrew press kit: facts, boilerplate, team, portraits and approved logos." ogTitle="Caldrew | Press" ogDescription="Caldrew press kit.">
<section class="cd-page-header"><div class="cd-container"><p class="cd-eyebrow">Press</p><h1 class="cd-page-title">Press kit</h1><p class="cd-lede">Who we are, how we work, the people behind the firm, and approved portraits and logos. Everything on this page is cleared for publication.</p></div></section><section class="cd-numbered"><div class="cd-container"><div class="cd-numbered-grid"><div><h2 class="cd-press-h2">At a glance</h2></div><div class="cd-press-facts"><div class="cd-press-fact"><p class="cd-press-fact-label">Name</p><p class="cd-press-fact-value">Caldrew. Legal entity: Caldrew, S.A.</p></div><div class="cd-press-fact"><p class="cd-press-fact-label">Founded</p><p class="cd-press-fact-value">2026, in Lisbon</p></div><div class="cd-press-fact"><p class="cd-press-fact-label">Founding partners</p><p class="cd-press-fact-value">João de Sousa Aroso and Manuel Queiroz Pereira</p></div><div class="cd-press-fact"><p class="cd-press-fact-label">What we do</p><p class="cd-press-fact-value">An investor, led by operators. We acquire established businesses and stay to build them.</p></div><div class="cd-press-fact"><p class="cd-press-fact-label">Where</p><p class="cd-press-fact-value">Portugal, with Iberia as a broad horizon</p></div><div class="cd-press-fact"><p class="cd-press-fact-label">Sectors</p><p class="cd-press-fact-value">Industrial and services businesses in fragmented markets</p></div><div class="cd-press-fact"><p class="cd-press-fact-label">Office</p><p class="cd-press-fact-value">Rua Castilho, 32 - 4, 1250-070 Lisboa</p></div><div class="cd-press-fact"><p class="cd-press-fact-label">Web</p><p class="cd-press-fact-value">caldrew.com</p></div><div class="cd-press-fact"><p class="cd-press-fact-label">Press</p><p class="cd-press-fact-value"><a href="mailto:enquiries@caldrew.com">enquiries@caldrew.com</a></p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="cd-numbered"><div class="cd-container"><div class="cd-numbered-grid"><div><h2 class="cd-press-h2">Boilerplate</h2><p class="cd-contact-note">Two lengths, in English and Portuguese. Use as written.</p></div><div><p class="cd-press-label cd-press-first">English, short</p><div class="cd-press-band"><p class="cd-p">Caldrew is an investor based in Lisbon, led by operators. It acquires established businesses in Iberia and stays to build them, growing platform companies in fragmented sectors acquisition by acquisition. Caldrew was founded in 2026 by João de Sousa Aroso and Manuel Queiroz Pereira. Its partners have run, turned around and sold companies themselves.</p></div><p class="cd-press-label">English, long</p><div class="cd-press-band"><p class="cd-p">Caldrew is an investor based in Lisbon, led by operators. It acquires established businesses in Iberia and stays to build them.</p><p class="cd-p">Caldrew acquires platform companies in fragmented industrial and services sectors and builds around them, acquisition by acquisition. It works with founders and families at a turning point: succession without an obvious successor, a transition that deserves a careful owner, or the need for a partner in the next phase of growth. Scale is earned through discipline, not financial engineering, and Caldrew holds for as long as that work takes.</p><p class="cd-p">The firm was founded in 2026 by João de Sousa Aroso, who founded and sold Leadzai and earlier led the acquisition, turnaround and sale of Páginas Amarelas, and Manuel Queiroz Pereira, a family office principal with 20 years of investment experience in Portugal. </p></div><p class="cd-press-label">Português, versão curta</p><div class="cd-press-band"><p class="cd-p">A Caldrew é uma investidora sediada em Lisboa, liderada por quem já geriu empresas. Compra empresas ibéricas estabelecidas e fica para as fazer crescer, desenvolvendo empresas plataforma em setores fragmentados, aquisição a aquisição. Foi fundada em 2026 por João de Sousa Aroso e Manuel Queiroz Pereira. Os seus sócios já geriram, recuperaram e venderam empresas. </p></div><p class="cd-press-label">Português, versão longa</p><div class="cd-press-band"><p class="cd-p">A Caldrew é uma investidora sediada em Lisboa, liderada por quem já geriu empresas. Compra empresas ibéricas estabelecidas e fica para as fazer crescer.</p><p class="cd-p">Compra empresas plataforma em setores industriais e de serviços fragmentados e constrói à volta delas, aquisição a aquisição. Trabalha com fundadores e famílias num momento de viragem: uma sucessão sem sucessor evidente, uma transição que merece um dono cuidadoso, ou a necessidade de um parceiro para a fase seguinte de crescimento. A escala ganha-se com disciplina, não com engenharia financeira, e a Caldrew mantém as participações durante o tempo que esse trabalho exigir.</p><p class="cd-p">Foi fundada em 2026 por João de Sousa Aroso, que fundou e vendeu a Leadzai e antes liderou a aquisição, recuperação e venda das Páginas Amarelas, e por Manuel Queiroz Pereira, responsável por um family office com 20 anos de experiência de investimento em Portugal. </p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="cd-numbered-how-we-work"><div class="cd-container"><div class="cd-press-rule"><h2 class="cd-press-h2 cd-press-stack">How we work</h2><div class="cd-grid"><div class="cd-card"><h3 class="cd-card-title">Operators, not financiers</h3><p class="cd-body">Our partners have run, turned around and sold companies themselves. We make decisions the way owners do, because we have been owners.</p></div><div class="cd-card"><h3 class="cd-card-title">Long horizons</h3><p class="cd-body">We buy to build. Good companies become leaders over years, and we hold for as long as that work takes.</p></div><div class="cd-card"><h3 class="cd-card-title">Growth by consolidation</h3><p class="cd-body">We acquire platform companies in fragmented sectors and build around them, acquisition by acquisition. Scale is earned through discipline, not financial engineering.</p></div><div class="cd-card"><h3 class="cd-card-title">Why Iberia</h3><p class="cd-body">Industrial and services markets remain fragmented. A generation of founders is reaching succession with no obvious buyer. And there is a persistent gap between what small companies and larger ones are worth.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="cd-numbered"><div class="cd-container"><div class="cd-press-rule"><h2 class="cd-press-h2 cd-press-stack">Team</h2></div><div class="cd-team-grid"><div><img class="cd-portrait" src="/images/jsa.jpeg" alt="Portrait of João de Sousa Aroso" loading="lazy"/><h2 class="cd-member-name">João de Sousa Aroso</h2><p class="cd-member-role">Founding Partner</p><p class="cd-member-bio">Founded Leadzai and led it as CEO through its sale. Earlier, he led the acquisition, turnaround and sale of Páginas Amarelas, the kind of work Caldrew now does as a firm. He also serves on the board of Erakulis.</p><a class="cd-cta-tight" href="/images/jsa.jpeg" download>Download portrait</a></div><div><img class="cd-portrait" src="/images/mqp.jpeg" alt="Portrait of Manuel Queiroz Pereira" loading="lazy"/><h2 class="cd-member-name">Manuel Queiroz Pereira</h2><p class="cd-member-role">Founding Partner</p><p class="cd-member-bio">A family office principal with 20 years of investment experience across sectors in Portugal. As co-founder of Caldrew, he brings an owner&#x27;s perspective, shaped by investing his own capital, with a focus on disciplined capital allocation and long-term value creation.</p><a class="cd-cta-tight" href="/images/mqp.jpeg" download>Download portrait</a></div><div><img class="cd-portrait" src="/images/jb.jpeg" alt="Portrait of João Bento" loading="lazy"/><h2 class="cd-member-name">João Bento</h2><p class="cd-member-role">Non-Executive Partner</p><p class="cd-member-bio">Former CEO of CTT, where he led the company&#x27;s transformation from Portugal&#x27;s postal operator into a leading Iberian logistics group. Earlier he ran Efacec and Grupo Manuel Champalimaud, and was COO of Brisa. As Non-Executive Partner, he brings the judgement of a career spent leading companies at scale.</p><a class="cd-cta-tight" href="/images/jb.jpeg" download>Download portrait</a></div><div><img class="cd-portrait" src="/images/hmc.jpeg" alt="Portrait of Hugo Martins da Costa" loading="lazy"/><h2 class="cd-member-name">Hugo Martins da Costa</h2><p class="cd-member-role">Chief Financial Officer</p><p class="cd-member-bio">Hugo leads Caldrew&#x27;s finance function: the reporting, structure and governance that long-term ownership depends on. He held director roles at Banco BIG and Banco Finantia, and taught as an assistant professor, bringing the discipline of someone who has worked deals from the numbers up.</p><a class="cd-cta-tight" href="/images/hmc.jpeg" download>Download portrait</a></div><div><img class="cd-portrait" src="/images/dcg.jpeg" alt="Portrait of Duarte Gonçalves" loading="lazy"/><h2 class="cd-member-name">Duarte Gonçalves</h2><p class="cd-member-role">Investment Analyst</p><p class="cd-member-bio">Duarte supports Caldrew&#x27;s investment work: sourcing, valuation, modelling and the analysis behind each deal. He came up in M&amp;A and transaction advisory, earlier at Beresford Capital and Haitong, and holds a Master&#x27;s in Finance from Católica Lisbon.</p><a class="cd-cta-tight" href="/images/dcg.jpeg" download>Download portrait</a></div></div></div></section><section class="cd-numbered"><div class="cd-container"><div class="cd-press-rule"><h2 class="cd-press-h2 cd-press-stack">Logos</h2><div class="cd-press-logos"><div><div class="cd-press-ground"><img class="cd-press-logo-img" src="/images/caldrew-logo.png" alt="Caldrew logo in ink, for light backgrounds" loading="lazy"/></div><p class="cd-press-fact-value">Logo for light backgrounds</p><p class="cd-press-meta">PNG, transparent, 837 × 192</p><a class="cd-cta-tight" href="/images/caldrew-logo.png" download>Download</a></div><div><div class="cd-press-ground cd-press-ink"><img class="cd-press-logo-img" src="/images/caldrew-logo-cream.png" alt="Caldrew logo in cream, for dark backgrounds" loading="lazy"/></div><p class="cd-press-fact-value">Logo for dark backgrounds</p><p class="cd-press-meta">PNG, transparent, 836 × 192</p><a class="cd-cta-tight" href="/images/caldrew-logo-cream.png" download>Download</a></div><div><div class="cd-press-ground cd-press-sand"><img class="cd-press-logo-img cd-press-tall" src="/images/caldrew-logo-plate.png" alt="Caldrew logo on a cream plate" loading="lazy"/></div><p class="cd-press-fact-value">Logo on plate, for any background</p><p class="cd-press-meta">PNG, 933 × 288</p><a class="cd-cta-tight" href="/images/caldrew-logo-plate.png" download>Download</a></div><div><div class="cd-press-ground"><img class="cd-press-logo-img cd-press-tall" src="/images/caldrew-mark-ink-512.png" alt="Caldrew mark" loading="lazy"/></div><p class="cd-press-fact-value">Mark, for avatars and small spaces</p><p class="cd-press-meta">PNG, 512 × 512</p><a class="cd-cta-tight" href="/images/caldrew-mark-ink-512.png" download>Download</a></div></div><p class="cd-press-label">Usage</p><p class="cd-body">Use the files as supplied. Don’t recolour, stretch, rotate or redraw the logo, and don’t add a tagline. Use the cream version only on dark backgrounds; when you can’t control the background, use the plate. The mark stands in for the logo where the full name can’t be read. In running text the name is Caldrew; Caldrew, S.A. is the legal entity.</p></div></div></section><section class="cd-section-ink"><div class="cd-container"><p class="cd-eyebrow-light">Press contact</p><h2 class="cd-band-title">Start a conversation.</h2><p class="cd-band-body">For interviews, comment or images, write to us.</p><a class="cd-press-mail" href="mailto:enquiries@caldrew.com">enquiries@caldrew.com</a></div></section>

</Base>
